From 0d66ae8c5e0814da5962d673ea394c648f5d152d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:28:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 055/120] render: HDR scenes render in half float and bloom
 with WE's HDR chain; FBOs take their format
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485 (the headless decompile; constants read from the binary):

- general.hdr is general flag 0x400 (setter GH 0x1401c95e0). bloomhdrstrength/threshold/feather/
  scatter/iterations are general +0x388/+0x38c/+0x390/+0x394/+0x398 (key table GH 0x1401c7880);
  their defaults 2, 1, 0.1, 1.619, 8, and bloomstrength 2 / bloomthreshold 0.65 (LWE had 0 / 0),
  are in the scene constructor GH 0x1401b6c60.
- The scene tick GH 0x1401afbf0 loads, with the renderer's HDR flag (0x2000), combine_hdr_upsample,
  combine_srgb, hdr_downsample, hdr_downsample_bloom, hdr_upsample and hdr_upsample_cubic instead
  of the LDR chain's materials, which are not built then.
- Targets (GH 0x1401af5b0): with HDR the scene is RGB161616f and one bloom level per halving of
  the smaller side, up to 8, "_rt_" + (2 << level) + "FrameBuffer", RGB161616f.
- GH 0x1401b42b0: levels = min (bloomhdriterations, levels made), at least 1; the downsample's
  g_BloomStrength = strength / (scatter^(max (levels, 2) − 2) + 1) (the call at 0x1401b436a is
  powf: inferred from its CRT shape), blend = (t, t − t·f, 2·t·f, 0.25 / (t·f + 1e-5)), tint;
  both upsamples' scatter.
- GH 0x1401b3b10: level 0 is hdr_downsample_bloom from the scene, levels 1… hdr_downsample from
  the level above, g_RenderVar0 = (1, 1, −1, −1) · 2^level / the scene size; then up from the
  last level, adding onto the one above (additive), hdr_upsample_cubic for the two coarsest
  steps, hdr_upsample after, g_RenderVar0 · 2^level; the combine reads the scene and level 0.
- FBO formats: an effect FBO's `format` (GH 0x140216080, names → enum GH 0x1402116c0, the .tex
  enum): rgba_backbuffer is RGBA16161616f with HDR else rgba8888, rgb_backbuffer RGB161616f /
  RGB888; image composites are RGBA16161616f with HDR (format 0xe), else RGBA8.

Ours: CFBO allocates the format it is given (rg88 → RG8, r8 → R8, the f formats half float, RGB
ones RGBA16F with alpha read as 1); FBOProvider maps the names. An HDR scene's FBO, composites,
compose targets and sampling copies are RGBA16F (LWE keeps alpha: compose layers and blend modes
read it). The HDR chain is a bloom image like the LDR one, one virtual effect per level count;
CScene feeds its uniforms each frame. The combine is WE's combine_hdr_upsample_linear (no lin ()):
WE's combine_hdr / combine_srgb apply lin () and multiply by g_RenderVar0.x for its sRGB
backbuffer view, which leaves the picture as it was (inferred: we write to an RGBA8 target
without sRGB encoding). The output copy to the host's framebuffer clamps, as WE's saturate does.

Inferred, not WE's: WE runs the HDR path only when its "postprocessing" setting is "ultra"
(GH 0x14013f860 sets the renderer flag 0x2000 from it, 0x6000 for "displayhdr"); LWE has no such
setting, so a general.hdr scene renders HDR unless WPENGINE_HDR=0. How general.hdr gates the
renderer flag was not found. bloomhdriterations is read at load.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B13 (E35, E23)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
